    "body": "## Problem\n\nUpward `find()` searches with string or table names always `stat` symlink targets. They ignore `follow=false`, cannot match links by type, and skip broken links, unlike predicate and downward searches.\n\n## Solution\n\nUse `lstat()` first and `stat` symlink targets only with `follow=true`. Retain the link type when target resolution fails. Extend the existing symlink test with focused upward name searches and a dangling link.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Probably need `follow = true` in `runtime/lua/vim/_core/exrc.lua` so that it still finds symlinked `.nvim.lua` . \r\n\r\nnews-breaking item?\r\n\r\n```\r\n• |vim.fs.find()| `type` matches symlinks as type=\"link\", unless `follow=true` is set.\r\n  Upward searches previously always followed symlinks.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nthen LGTM",
            "created_at": "2026-10-19T18:42:17Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42417#issuecomment-6274595281",
            "id": 6274595281,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/42417",
